---
title: Japanese Chicken Rice in Rice Cooker
servings: 4
course: dinner
tags: quick, one-pan, chicken, rice
image: https://www.marmiton.org/assets/images/default-recipe-picture_80x80-6PRRwF3.jpg
source: https://www.marmiton.org/recettes/recette_riz-poulet-japonais-au-rice-cooker_224166.aspx
prep time: 15m
cook time: 15m
---

Wash the @sushi rice{400%g}, then let it soak for ~{15%minutes} in cold water.

Cut the @chicken thigh{200%g}, @carrot{1} and @mushroom{100%g}.

In the #rice cooker{}, add the @&sushi rice{}, @soy sauce{50%ml}, @mirin{4%tbsp}, @sugar{20%g}, @water{600%ml}, @&mushroom{} and @&carrot{}. Mix.

Add the @&chicken thigh{} on top without mixing.

Turn on the #rice cooker{}.
